<title>INDIA: Indian soybean firm, meal steady, oil up.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean firm, meal steady, oil up.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean pries were firm on good purchasing from processing plants on MOnday,d ealers said. Prices were up by 100-200 rupees per tonne. Business volume was dull and the undertone was firm.</p>
<p>Soyoil solvent was up by 100 rupees per tonne on limited supplies while soyoil refined was steady in thin trading. Business volume was dull and the undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices remained steady in very limited trading. Soymeal yellow was $265-266 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) west Indian ports for export. Rapeseed extraction was $96-97 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) in bulk for export and was 3,225-3,250 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on Rail) condition. The undertone was steady.</p>
